{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From French {{term|carobe|lang=fr}}, ultimately from Arabic {{term|الخروب||locust bean pod|tr=kharrub|lang=ar}}, from Assyrian [[kharubu]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[evergreen]] [[shrub]] or [[tree]], ''Ceratonia siliqua'',  native to the [[Mediterranean]] region.
# the fruit of that tree.
# a sweet chocolate-like confection made with the pulp of the fruit.

====Synonyms====
* [[St. John's bread]]
* [[locust bean]]

